  "title": "Restricted-Sumset Saturation with Two Missing Sums in Prime Fields",
  "batch_label": "87",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every prime p >= 11 and every integer 3 <= ell <= (p-3)/2, every ordered pair (A,B) of subsets of F_p with |B|=ell, |A|=p-ell, and |A dotplus B|=p-2 is simultaneously affinely equivalent to (A_(a,b),B_(a,b)) for some nonnegative a,b with a+b=ell, with B_(a,b)={-2j:0<=j<a} union {1+2j:0<=j<b}, C_(a,b)={2+2j:0<=j<a} union {-1-2j:0<=j<b}, and A_(a,b)=F_p minus C_(a,b). Every displayed pair has missing restricted sums exactly {0,2}. Two displayed representatives are affinely equivalent if and only if (a,b) agrees up to swapping, so there are floor(ell/2)+1 affine classes.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
